   "he": "עֵד אֶחָד עִבְרִי וְעֵד אֶחָד יְוָנִי. וְלִיתַּכְשַׁר הַאי בְּעֵד אֶחָד עִבְרִי וְעֵד אֶחָד יְוָנִי, וְהַאי בְּעֵד אֶחָד עִבְרִי וְעֵד אֶחָד יְוָנִי – דְּהָא תְּנַן: עֵד אֶחָד עִבְרִי וְעֵד אֶחָד יְוָנִי – כָּשֵׁר!",
   "en": "§ It is stated in the mishna that if «one witness» signed in «Hebrew and» then «one witness» signed in «Greek,» and then one more witness signed in Hebrew and one in Greek, both bills of divorce are invalid. The Gemara asks: «But let this» bill of divorce «be validated by one Hebrew witness and one Greek witness, and that» bill of divorce be validated «by» the other pair composed of «one Hebrew witness and one Greek witness. Didn’t we learn» in the subsequent mishna that a bill of divorce that was signed by «one witness» in «Hebrew and one witness» in «Greek is valid?»"
  }
